# Copy to .dev.vars for local `wrangler dev`. NEVER commit .dev.vars — it is
# gitignored. In production these are Worker secrets:
#
#   wrangler secret put SAM_API_KEY
#   wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#
# Note that `wrangler dev` works with neither of these set: the Worker falls
# back to the bundled fixture in fixtures/hand-written.json. That is the mode to
# develop the frontend in, because a cold local cache otherwise spends six
# SAM.gov requests out of roughly ten per day on every fresh session.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAM_API_KEY
#
# sam.gov → sign in (via Login.gov) → Account Details → Public API Key.
# Displayed once — paste it into a password manager before navigating away.
# No entity registration needed; a personal account is enough.
#
# Two things that cost an hour each on day one:
#
#   1. The working endpoint is  https://api.sam.gov/prod/opportunities/v2/search
#      The documented form WITHOUT /prod/ returns 404. `npm run probe` resolves
#      this empirically rather than trusting either.
#
#   2. cmd.exe's `set SAM_API_KEY="abc"` stores the QUOTES as part of the value.
#      A 40-character key becomes 42 and api.data.gov rejects it with a bare
#      404 — indistinguishable from a dead endpoint. Use no quotes in cmd, or
#      use PowerShell, where $env:SAM_API_KEY="abc" does the right thing.
#      `src/lib/apiKey.ts` strips them and warns, but the shell is the real fix.
#
# Budget: roughly 10 requests/day on a public key, and api.data.gov sends no
# X-RateLimit headers on this endpoint, so the only visibility is the counter
# this Worker keeps itself — see /api/health.
SAM_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#
# console.anthropic.com → API keys. Set a hard spend limit while you are there;
# it takes two minutes and is the difference between a bad night and a bad month.
#
# Used by the Worker for scoring, and by `npm run score` — the offline harness
# that measures the prompt against fixtures/labels.json. The harness is where
# prompt changes should be evaluated; it needs this key but no SAM.gov key,
# because it hydrates descriptions through the deployed Worker.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
